\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs22\lang9 A plant shop must take into account different things.\par
1. \b0 A good place to sell. You can definitely use your parents ' small garden, but that's living under their control. Here you can use that to make a known name.\par
Or buy , rent a place. Where you will have access to a storefront and more people will come on average. More space and more trust.\par
You have a trust meter (percentages of how probable for customers to pick you.\par
You have money bar.\par
You have experience and skill level that enables more flowers, better revenue, more trust etc.\par
You have demand, curated by trust meter. \par
\b 2. Selling\b0 . Selling depends on the health of the plant, plant type, prices are set automatically. \par
You can also learn from books on the subject or from word of mouth here and there.\par
You need to spend time to hone your skills, giving you better revenue, unlocking new flower types and gaining more trust.\par
You also have DEMAND: realizing what flowers sell best in what season. This can be solved also by having help from someone. Different seasons, cities, cultures demand differing plant needs. \par
You can buy flower things from other shops, or, if you know, suppliers, especially ones with connection to London and the outside. Otherwise, you ll have access to a variety of everyday seeds. \par
London and Paris. has more fierce competition, more expensive storefronts and things are harder, you need to find a niche. \par
The more healthy the plant, the better the revenue off of it. The faster its growth.\par
\b 3.\b0\par
-you need seeds, water, dirt, pots and constant attention spent on taking care of flower:\par
>periodical change of the earth\par
